    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** headlining the offense, boasting a team-high 83.29 score. His matchup against the right-handed Avila is prime for production, bolstered by a significant +16% park factor and +19% advantage against the starter\u2019s xERA. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** remains an anchor at 81.41, poised to exploit JP Sears\u2019 vulnerable 4.65 xERA in what should be a high-upside environment. Meanwhile, **Jackson Merrill**, **Andy Pages**, and **Cole Carrigg** offer elite efficiency\u2014all scoring above 70.00\u2014thanks to favorable platoon dynamics and the speed-heavy nature of their matchups against pitchers who struggle to neutralize stolen base attempts. **Josh Lowe** specifically warrants attention; his 67.37 score is elevated by a \"slow delivery\" bonus from the opposition, which maximizes his SB potential in our scarcity-focused build.\n\nThe decision to keep **Heliot Ramos** on the bench was the most difficult call of the day. Despite a solid 54.25 score and the added benefit of a stolen base threat against a slow-moving pitcher, he was edged out by the superior floor and higher situational ceilings provided by **Miguel Vargas** and **Drake Baldwin**. **Miguel Vargas** carries a score of 63.53 into his start, justified by an elite 0.402 xwOBA that signals positive regression, while **Drake Baldwin** earns his start behind the plate due to a favorable matchup against Kyle Leahy. We are monitoring **Jorge Polanco** closely, though he remains benched not only due to lower projected output but also a 38% rain risk that introduces unnecessary variance. Managers should note that while several lineup slots remain \"Pending,\" the projected order for **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Kyle Tucker**, and **Jackson Merrill** is locked into high-leverage spots, provided no late scratches emerge.",
